Package: bigballR
Type: Package
Title: NCAA Women's Basketball Data Analysis Functionality
Version: 0.2.0
Author: Jake Flancer (original), Derek Willis (WBB adaptation)
Maintainer: Derek Willis <dwillis@gmail.com>
Description: This package gives users the ability to work with NCAA Women's Basketball data in a clean and detailed manner.
    The functions included can retrieve and manipulate NCAA play-by-play data, giving users a variety of ways to find insights
    about their favorite players and teams. An especially important feature is the ability to report who is on the court
    at each event in the play-by-play, opening up many possible areas of analysis. Adapted from the original bigballR package
    for men's basketball to support women's basketball data.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 3.1.2)
LazyData: true
Imports:
    dplyr,
    XML,
    stringr,
    magrittr,
    ggplot2,
    igraph,
    ggraph,
    gtools,
    rvest,
    jsonlite,
    glue
